Name:Rules pilot 466 - Kill Thalia before the burn
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Hard
Description:It is your second main phase. You control no creatures and have Mogg Fanatic, Lightning Bolt and Shock in hand, with three red mana floating. The opponent is at 5 life and controls an untapped Thalia, Guardian of Thraben (2/1 first strike; noncreature spells cost {1} more). Reduce the opponent to 0 life this turn.
Rule:authored-cost-increase-removed-first | A cost increase is applied as each spell's total cost is determined (CR 601.2f), so removing Thalia first makes the rest cheaper: cast Mogg Fanatic (a creature, untaxed), sacrifice it to kill Thalia, then Bolt and Shock for one red each, 5 damage; with Thalia alive the burn costs two each and three mana deal at most 4
